# android/prover-assets.sha256 — ADR-0010 prover-asset integrity manifest.
#
# Each line maps a file under android/app/src/main/assets/prover/ to its
# pinned SHA-256. The `verifyProverAssets` Gradle task in
# android/app/build.gradle.kts hashes every file in the directory and
# fails the build if a digest does not match what's pinned here.
#
# Bumping the snarkjs / circuit assets is a 2-file PR:
#   1. drop the new bundle into android/app/src/main/assets/prover/
#   2. update both this file AND adr/0010-android-webview-snarkjs-bundling.md
#
# The dual update is intentional — ADR-0010 is the audit-side source of
# truth; this file is the build-side enforcement. CI runs the same
# verify task so a digest drift on either side stops the build.
#
# Format: `<filename>=<lowercase hex sha256>`. Comments and blank lines
# are ignored. NO commas, no quoting. The parser in build.gradle.kts is
# intentionally trivial so an attacker can't sneak a digest in via a
# weird key/value encoding.

